# Staging vs production (musician-ai-studio)

TestFlight testers and live web users are **production**. Daily dev uses a **separate staging API** so backend + frontend changes do not hit testers until you ship.

## Environments

| | **Staging** | **Production** |
|---|-------------|----------------|
| Git branch | `staging` | `main` |
| API | Vercel preview for `staging` branch (`config/environments.json`) | `https://www.nabadai.com` |
| Web users | Preview URL only (not nabadai.com) | nabadai.com |
| iOS simulator | `npm run sim` (bakes **staging** API into bundled `www/`) | — |
| TestFlight / live iPhone prod | — | Archive/install with **production** env |
| Supabase | **Shared today** — same DB unless Preview env vars point to a staging project | Production project |

**Backend code** is isolated per branch (staging push → preview deploy; main push → production). **Database** is still shared until a second Supabase project is wired in Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables → **Preview**.

## Daily workflow (default)

1. **`git checkout staging`** — all feature/fix work commits here.
2. Change code (`src/`, `api/`, etc.).
3. **`npm run sim`** — sync www, bake **staging** `env.client.js`, build simulator. Safe for backend + frontend iteration.
4. **`git push origin staging`** — deploys **staging API only** (Vercel preview). Does **not** affect TestFlight or nabadai.com.

Do **not** push to `main` while testers are on TestFlight unless shipping.

## Ship to TestFlight + production (when approved)

1. Merge **`staging` → `main`** (or cherry-pick); resolve conflicts on `main`.
2. **`npm run stamp:build`** — bump build id + sync `www/`.
3. **`npm run env:production`** — bake production API into `env.client.js` before any TestFlight/device prod install.
4. **`git add` / `commit` / `git push origin main`** — deploys production web + API.
5. **TestFlight**: Archive in Xcode (Release) or approved `run:ios` with production env — **never** ship a TestFlight build baked with staging API.
6. Run any **Supabase SQL** on production project before or with the API deploy if the release depends on new RPCs/tables.

## Commands

- `npm run env:staging` — point bundled iOS/web native env at staging API
- `npm run env:production` — point at nabadai.com (TestFlight / prod device)
- `npm run sim` — **staging** simulator preview (default for agents after app changes)
- `npm run run:ios` — physical device; use **`npm run env:production`** first if matching TestFlight

## Agent rules

- **Default branch for changes:** `staging`, not `main`.
- **Default simulator command:** `npm run sim` (staging API).
- **Before `git push origin main`:** user must explicitly approve shipping to production/TestFlight.
- **Backend + DB on staging:** OK to push `staging` branch; call out that **shared Supabase** means SQL migrations still affect live data until a staging DB exists.
- Update `config/environments.json` → `staging.apiBase` if the Vercel preview URL differs after first deploy.
